# Display attribution, not history rewriting.
#
# On 2026-09-11 at 17:52, the COD3S platform's release script
# (`.gitlab/post_release_tag.sh`) was run by hand on a developer machine. It
# set its bot tagger identity with `git config --global`, so every commit made
# on that machine for the next six days carries
# "COD3S release bot <ci@edgemind.net>" as its author. Forty-one of them are
# in this repository, six of those on master, including the 5.4.0 release
# commit. None of it is the bot's work.
#
# This file fixes what `git log`, `git blame` and `git shortlog` display,
# without touching a single commit: rewriting a shared history would cost more
# than the wrong attribution.
#
# No side effect: the release bot only posts tags, never commits, and tags do
# not go through mailmap. The cause is closed upstream (the platform job now
# passes its identity through the environment, with tests pinning it).
Roland Donat <roland.donat@edgemind.net> <ci@edgemind.net>
